# The same program as examples/statement.vine, not one character changed,
# over a second month's file. That claim is what read() was bought on and
# nothing had tested it; here it is structural rather than asserted, because
# there is one program file and this case names it.
#
# April's export came out of an upgraded tool. Its header is capitalised, its
# columns are in a different order, it has a Currency column the program has
# never heard of, and its lines end the way a Windows machine ends them.
#
# The input lives here rather than in examples/ because the runner names a
# case's `.in` after the case: a second input for one program needs a second
# file to name it.
examples/statement.vine
